#=GF RT N-myc translation is initiated via an internal ribosome entry segment that
#=GF RT displays enhanced activity in neuronal cells.
#=GF RA Jopling CL, Willis AE
#=GF RL Oncogene 2001;20:2664-2670.
#=GF CC This family represents the n-myc internal ribosome entry site (IRES). The
#=GF CC myc family of genes when expressed are known to be involved in the control
#=GF CC of cell growth, differentiation and apoptosis. n-myc mRNA has an
#=GF CC alternative method of translation via internal ribosome entry where
#=GF CC ribosomes are recruited to the IRES located in the 5' UTR thus bypassing
#=GF CC the typical eukaryotic cap-dependent translation pathway [1].
#=GF WK n-myc_internal_ribosome_entry_site_(IRES)
#=GF SQ 6

